\# CoSTA_monitor.wpi
# Witty Pi 4 schedule for deployment
# Loaded by CoSTA.sh at every start-up, but only when started by CoSTA.service
#
# BEGIN / END: first and last day of the deployment (YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS, Pi time = HST)
#   the cycle counts from BEGIN: with BEGIN at 00:00:00 and a 30 min interval,
#   the Pi wakes at :00 and :30 every hour
# ON / OFF: how long the Pi is on and off in each cycle, ON + OFF = interval
#   units: D days, H hours, M minutes, S seconds (e.g. ON M2 + OFF M28 = every 30 min,
#   ON M2 + OFF M58 = every hour, ON M2 + OFF H5 M58 = every 6 hours)
#   ON must be longer than boot + one CoSTA cycle, or the Witty Pi cuts the power mid-cycle
#   ON M2: to be measured and changed during testing
#
# After editing: save in /home/kaja/wittypi/schedules/ 
# (SCHEDULE in CoSTA.conf = this file name)

BEGIN 2026-10-01 00:00:00
END   2026-12-16 09:00:00
ON    M2
OFF   M28
